Bluetooth: allow an explicit local module package version

Retain upstream MODULE_VERSION unless source preparation supplies a local
BT_BACKPORT_VERSION. A distinct, newer numeric version allows DKMS 2.8.7
to install a local backport without its same-version skip or --force.
This identifies the package; it does not claim support for another ABI.

Source: Linux 7.2 drivers/bluetooth/{btusb,btmtk}.c
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

--- a/btusb.c
+++ b/btusb.c
@@ -4755,1 +4755,5 @@
+#ifdef BT_BACKPORT_VERSION
+MODULE_VERSION(BT_BACKPORT_VERSION);
+#else
 MODULE_VERSION(VERSION);
+#endif
--- a/btmtk.c
+++ b/btmtk.c
@@ -1650,1 +1650,5 @@
+#ifdef BT_BACKPORT_VERSION
+MODULE_VERSION(BT_BACKPORT_VERSION);
+#else
 MODULE_VERSION(VERSION);
+#endif
